WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.566 --> 00:00:06.466
Welcome back to Pokévision Live! Time for more rankings!

2
00:00:06.533 --> 00:00:09.000
We’ve reached number four on our top ten!

3
00:00:09.066 --> 00:00:11.500
And it’s Snow-Capped Onix!

4
00:00:11.566 --> 00:00:13.666
Never seen Pokévision before!

5
00:00:13.733 --> 00:00:16.500
That’s amazing, since everyone knows about it!

6
00:00:16.566 --> 00:00:20.500
Pokévision refers to promotional videos created by Trainers themselves.

7
00:00:20.566 --> 00:00:24.133
Awesome! That sounds so cool! I wish I knew what that meant.

8
00:00:25.566 --> 00:00:31.799
Next up, we bring you video number three, which is Psyduck at Twilight!

9
00:00:31.866 --> 00:00:35.133
Pokévision is a way for Trainers to introduce their Pokémon.

10
00:00:35.199 --> 00:00:36.900
Psyduck’s such a cutie pie!

11
00:00:36.966 --> 00:00:40.733
Next, number two! The Beauty of Joy!

12
00:00:42.533 --> 00:00:46.633
It can also show the bond between Trainer and Pokémon, like this video does!

13
00:00:46.699 --> 00:00:50.366
You see, Trainers upload their videos to an online viewing site

14
00:00:50.433 --> 00:00:54.433
and the Pokévision Top Ten is based on the viewer rankings they receive.

15
00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:58.533
And now it’s time for this week’s video number one!

16
00:00:58.599 --> 00:01:01.099
Aria and Fennekin’s Life of an Idol!

17
00:01:01.166 --> 00:01:04.833
- I knew Aria would be number one!
- Na-na!

18
00:01:04.899 --> 00:01:08.899
After those two had a series of top ten Pokévision appearances,

19
00:01:08.966 --> 00:01:13.333
they made their debut as a pop duo and became Pokémon superstars!

20
00:01:14.399 --> 00:01:15.433
Chespin!

21
00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:16.733
- So cute!
- Na-na!

22
00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:19.266
- You know, Bonnie, that is a cute...
- Huh?

23
00:01:19.333 --> 00:01:21.233
..Fennekin.

24
00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:23.133
- Ches!
- I think Ash gets it!

25
00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:26.733
You know what? My Fennekin’s just as cute any day!

26
00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:30.000
For sure! And you’re at least as cute as Aria is.

27
00:01:30.066 --> 00:01:32.166
- Na-na!
- Bonnie, that’s so sweet!

28
00:01:32.233 --> 00:01:33.233
- Kin!
- Pin!

29
00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:36.566
You know, I’m pretty sure you can rent all the equipment you need

30
00:01:36.633 --> 00:01:38.699
to make Pokévision videos right here!

31
00:01:38.766 --> 00:01:43.899
Really? Perfect! So! I’ll make my debut Pokévision video!

32
00:01:43.966 --> 00:01:46.866
♪ I want to be the very best ♪

33
00:01:46.933 --> 00:01:49.500
♪ Like no one ever was ♪

34
00:01:50.633 --> 00:01:53.166
♪ To catch them is my real test ♪

35
00:01:53.233 --> 00:01:56.199
♪ To train them is my cause ♪

36
00:01:56.266 --> 00:01:59.266
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all It's you and me ♪

37
00:01:59.333 --> 00:02:02.533
♪ Pokémon! I know it's my destiny ♪

38
00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:05.966
♪ Pokémon! Yeah, you're my best friend ♪

39
00:02:06.033 --> 00:02:08.400
♪ In a world we must defend ♪

40
00:02:08.466 --> 00:02:10.900
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all ♪

41
00:02:10.966 --> 00:02:13.966
♪ Got to catch them all! Pokémon! ♪

42
00:02:23.633 --> 00:02:26.100
Now that our heroes have arrived at the Pokémon Center

43
00:02:26.166 --> 00:02:27.700
en route to Cyllage City,

44
00:02:27.766 --> 00:02:31.866
Serena has decided to make her debut Pokévision video!

45
00:02:31.933 --> 00:02:35.833
I always knew I’d be making a Pokévision video if I ever got a Pokémon!

46
00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:38.000
I want to make one with Dedenne!

47
00:02:38.066 --> 00:02:41.400
But I think you’ve forgotten Dedenne isn’t your Pokémon!

48
00:02:41.466 --> 00:02:45.200
All right, then I guess I’ll just have to make a video

49
00:02:45.266 --> 00:02:47.299
- to find a wife for you!
- Ah!

50
00:02:47.366 --> 00:02:49.533
Ash, will you help me with mine?

51
00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:52.200
Thing is, I want to do some special training

52
00:02:52.266 --> 00:02:54.433
so I can be ready for my battle with Grant.

53
00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:55.700
- Really?
- Yeah!

54
00:02:55.766 --> 00:03:01.200
If I don’t have a move to counter Onix’s Rock Tomb, there’s no way I can win.

55
00:03:01.266 --> 00:03:04.133
Special training would be the logical choice.

56
00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:05.533
- Right!
- Pika!

57
00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:09.233
- You’re really psyched!
- Well, maybe the rest of you can help me!

58
00:03:09.299 --> 00:03:11.299
- Sure!
- Ches!

59
00:03:11.366 --> 00:03:13.899
After you’ve finished shooting all the video footage you need,

60
00:03:13.966 --> 00:03:17.333
simply bring it back here and we’ll do all the necessary editing

61
00:03:17.399 --> 00:03:18.733
and create a soundtrack as well.

62
00:03:18.799 --> 00:03:20.633
That would be a big help!

63
00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.700
I could even do a video, too!

64
00:03:22.766 --> 00:03:26.500
Now, I think I can be the most helpful behind the scenes.

65
00:03:26.566 --> 00:03:30.133
No way! You’ll be the most help if we make you a big star!

66
00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:32.666
But I don’t want to be a star!

67
00:03:32.733 --> 00:03:36.600
We also have quite an extensive wardrobe department you can use.

68
00:03:36.666 --> 00:03:39.633
- That’ll be perfect!
- Yeah, I can’t wait!

69
00:03:42.066 --> 00:03:43.533
We’re all ready to roll!

70
00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:45.266
Then let’s go!

71
00:03:45.333 --> 00:03:47.533
-Chespin Pin!

72
00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:49.733
Scene one and action!

73
00:03:49.799 --> 00:03:53.133
Ahem. Uh... Hello there!

74
00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:57.233
- I’m Clemont and this is...
- Chespin!

75
00:03:57.299 --> 00:03:58.733
No, no! Cut, cut!

76
00:03:58.799 --> 00:04:02.000
- Chespin, you’re too far out front!
- Chespin?

77
00:04:02.066 --> 00:04:04.366
And, Clemont, you need more energy!

78
00:04:04.433 --> 00:04:07.933
Your voice is getting softer and softer!

79
00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:11.066
I told you! I’m not any good at this sort of thing,

80
00:04:11.133 --> 00:04:14.266
so why can’t we make Serena’s already?

81
00:04:14.333 --> 00:04:16.966
Hey, I’ve got an idea! Talk for him, Bonnie!

82
00:04:17.033 --> 00:04:18.366
You mean speak his lines?

83
00:04:18.433 --> 00:04:22.066
Uh-huh! You see, we’ll be hearing your voice instead of Clemont’s.

84
00:04:22.133 --> 00:04:25.133
Then all Clemont has to do is match his lips to everything you say!

85
00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:29.599
Ah! That might work! Yeah! Let’s give it a try!

86
00:04:29.666 --> 00:04:32.366
All right, take two. Action!

87
00:04:33.366 --> 00:04:37.566
Hello there. My name’s Clemont. I’d like you to meet my partners,

88
00:04:37.633 --> 00:04:39.033
- Chespin...
- Ches!

89
00:04:39.099 --> 00:04:42.700
..and Bunnelby!

90
00:04:42.766 --> 00:04:47.166
- Oh! I can’t stand this kind of video!
- Don’t worry.

91
00:04:47.233 --> 00:04:50.466
We’ll edit everything together later and that’ll make it perfect!

92
00:04:50.533 --> 00:04:54.533
- Now it’s time for our video debut!
- Fenn!

93
00:04:57.099 --> 00:04:58.733
Kin!

94
00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:02.200
First take a shot of Fennekin and me running through the field.

95
00:05:02.266 --> 00:05:03.833
Okay!

96
00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:07.900
It looks like that’s my cue! Hm!

97
00:05:07.966 --> 00:05:10.200
Because the future is now, thanks to science!

98
00:05:10.266 --> 00:05:12.700
Clemontic Gear on!

99
00:05:12.766 --> 00:05:16.700
I thought that we would encounter a situation precisely like this one!

100
00:05:16.766 --> 00:05:19.700
I call it the Pokéstar Shooter!

101
00:05:19.766 --> 00:05:22.233
- Pokéstar Shooter?
- Boring!

102
00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:26.233
My camera-equipped mobile tripod robot can provide fixed shots,

103
00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:28.266
mobile shots or even crane shots

104
00:05:28.333 --> 00:05:32.566
as high a quality as Pokéstar Studios, the movie capital of the world!

105
00:05:32.633 --> 00:05:36.466
This device will make you shine like stars! Device on!

106
00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:39.566
Huh?

107
00:05:39.633 --> 00:05:41.866
- Low angle!
- Fenn!

108
00:05:41.933 --> 00:05:43.566
- High angle!
- Huh?

109
00:05:43.633 --> 00:05:45.566
- Zoom in!
- Oh!

110
00:05:45.633 --> 00:05:47.766
You’re witnessing movie perfection!

111
00:05:47.833 --> 00:05:51.333
I guess science really is amazing, just like Ash says.

112
00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:55.066
This could be your first big hit in a while! Way to go, big brother!

113
00:05:55.133 --> 00:05:57.266
Na-na!

114
00:05:57.333 --> 00:06:01.833
All right, now to get that shot of Serena and Fennekin running through the field.

115
00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:04.066
- Ready!
- Fennekin!

116
00:06:04.133 --> 00:06:06.099
Okay, action!

117
00:06:09.033 --> 00:06:11.500
Huh?

118
00:06:11.566 --> 00:06:14.133
What happened? It’s out of control!

119
00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:20.133
Oh! Get away as fast as you can!

120
00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:23.133
If we’re going to stand a chance against Onix’s Rock Tomb,

121
00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:25.933
we’ll need a lot of speed! Pikachu can use Quick Attack

122
00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:29.133
and Froakie and Fletchling’s Double Team will make its attacks harder to hit!

123
00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:33.633
We’ll get your moves in tip-top shape and stop that Rock Tomb! Let’s do it!

124
00:06:35.466 --> 00:06:38.633
Great! Now let’s get moving. Come on!

125
00:06:44.666 --> 00:06:48.333
Huh? Looks like one of Clemont’s inventions at work.

126
00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:51.599
- Science is really amazing, isn’t it?!
- Pika! Pika!

127
00:06:51.666 --> 00:06:55.766
- It’s not amazing!
- My device is out of control!

128
00:06:55.833 --> 00:06:58.933
- Ash, do something!
- Right. Don’t worry!

129
00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:02.166
Pikachu, aim for the robot and use Electro Ball!

130
00:07:02.233 --> 00:07:05.900
Pikachu! Pik! Pika, Pika, Pika, Pika, Pik!

131
00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:12.599
Now look at me! I’m covered head to toe in black soot!

132
00:07:12.666 --> 00:07:15.599
But I thought you wanted me to help you out!

133
00:07:15.666 --> 00:07:19.033
- Fenn!
- Pika!

134
00:07:19.099 --> 00:07:21.766
Argh!

135
00:07:21.833 --> 00:07:25.566
Ah! You didn’t have to do that.

136
00:07:25.633 --> 00:07:30.066
Uh, if you remember, Fennekin likes to stay clean.

137
00:07:30.133 --> 00:07:33.799
You know, this might be the perfect time to have a wardrobe change!

138
00:07:33.866 --> 00:07:35.566
That’s a great idea!

139
00:07:35.633 --> 00:07:38.366
- Here I am!
- Kin!

140
00:07:40.366 --> 00:07:44.466
See how the Fennekin ears and tail give this outfit its charm?

141
00:07:44.533 --> 00:07:46.133
- So cute!
- Pika!

142
00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:48.666
Hey, Ash, please help us with the video!

143
00:07:48.733 --> 00:07:50.766
But we’ve got special training to do.

144
00:07:50.833 --> 00:07:54.966
Sometimes taking a break can go a long way to help you to focus your training!

145
00:07:55.033 --> 00:07:56.299
- Pika!
- You’re right!

146
00:07:56.366 --> 00:07:57.533
Yay!

147
00:07:57.599 --> 00:08:00.533
From now on, I’ll be manning the video camera!

148
00:08:01.733 --> 00:08:03.599
And action!

149
00:08:03.666 --> 00:08:06.799
- Fennekin!
- Fennekin!

150
00:08:06.866 --> 00:08:10.900
The next scene will be Serena and Fennekin baking goodies together.

151
00:08:10.966 --> 00:08:15.400
Ta-da! Notice! We’re wearing matching aprons!

152
00:08:15.466 --> 00:08:19.866
- And Pikachu’s got a cameo role!
- Pika, Pika.

153
00:08:19.933 --> 00:08:23.066
- Are we ready to roll?
- All set!

154
00:08:23.133 --> 00:08:25.599
And action!

155
00:08:28.866 --> 00:08:30.733
Fenn! Fenn!

156
00:08:30.799 --> 00:08:36.033
- Pikachu! Powdered sugar, please!
- Pikachu!

157
00:08:36.100 --> 00:08:39.633
Pik... Pik...

158
00:08:39.699 --> 00:08:41.366
Fenn!

159
00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:44.400
Pik.

160
00:08:44.466 --> 00:08:46.100
Fennekin!

161
00:08:46.166 --> 00:08:48.033
- Pik, Pik, Pik!
- We’re sorry, Fennekin!

162
00:08:48.100 --> 00:08:50.000
- Pika, Pika!
- Fenn!

163
00:08:50.066 --> 00:08:51.199
Ah!

164
00:08:51.266 --> 00:08:56.100
- I guess I just can’t win!
- Pikachu.

165
00:08:56.166 --> 00:08:58.866
Right. And cut.

166
00:08:59.866 --> 00:09:01.733
Fenn.

167
00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:04.333
It looks like Fennekin’s not mad anymore.

168
00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:06.833
Staying clean sure makes Fennekin happy!

169
00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:11.333
Fennekin’s always busy grooming, because getting dirty is so upsetting!

170
00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:14.000
I think you’re a bit like that too, Serena.

171
00:09:14.066 --> 00:09:16.633
Right! Like Fennekin, I love to keep clean!

172
00:09:16.699 --> 00:09:20.866
I like to look my best, so good grooming is always a must!

173
00:09:20.933 --> 00:09:24.466
- You two sure make quite a team.
- Pika, Pika!

174
00:09:25.766 --> 00:09:28.900
- And cut!
- We’ve got everything we need.

175
00:09:28.966 --> 00:09:33.066
So now we’ll just go and get that nice man to edit it all for us!

176
00:09:33.133 --> 00:09:36.266
So the twerps have Pokévision on the brain.

177
00:09:36.333 --> 00:09:39.100
Hm! Speaking as a professional actress,

178
00:09:39.166 --> 00:09:41.633
the twerps are making a monumental movie mess!

179
00:09:41.699 --> 00:09:44.833
Let’s use that mess to our advantage.

180
00:09:44.900 --> 00:09:47.000
- Use it?
- Use what?

181
00:09:47.066 --> 00:09:49.366
Just follow my lead!

182
00:09:49.433 --> 00:09:51.966
- We’re sure to succeed!
- Let's proceed!

183
00:09:52.033 --> 00:09:54.000
Wobbuffet!

184
00:09:54.066 --> 00:09:56.300
Who’s that Pokémon?

185
00:10:01.066 --> 00:10:03.133
It’s Bunnelby!

186
00:10:08.466 --> 00:10:11.199
What? The editing machine’s broken?

187
00:10:11.266 --> 00:10:14.133
- Oh! It can’t be!
- I’m afraid it’s true.

188
00:10:14.199 --> 00:10:18.199
I had only left the room for a minute, but when I came back in...

189
00:10:18.266 --> 00:10:19.600
What am I going to do?

190
00:10:19.666 --> 00:10:22.800
Do you really need to edit it, or can you leave it as it is?

191
00:10:22.866 --> 00:10:25.466
If we use raw footage, it’ll be a disaster!

192
00:10:25.533 --> 00:10:28.600
- Pokévision production, anyone?
- Huh?

193
00:10:28.666 --> 00:10:30.566
Inexpensive, yet reliable!

194
00:10:30.633 --> 00:10:34.100
Pokéstar quality on the cheap! We’ll give your video style

195
00:10:34.166 --> 00:10:37.033
- and we’ll do it with a smile!
- I don’t remember that place.

196
00:10:37.100 --> 00:10:41.533
We’re the Pokévision Rocketeers, the video experts in Pokéstar Studios!

197
00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:45.100
And we’ve decided to grace your town with our genius!

198
00:10:45.166 --> 00:10:48.366
Trainers who want their Pokévision production to be primo

199
00:10:48.433 --> 00:10:51.100
get top-tier treatment at our super-special studio!

200
00:10:51.166 --> 00:10:54.100
So you’re a Pokévision production company?

201
00:10:54.166 --> 00:10:57.000
Observant! Come in!

202
00:10:57.066 --> 00:11:00.633
The proof of our prowess needs to be seen to be believed!

203
00:11:00.699 --> 00:11:05.100
You’ll be so moved, you'll need to rent a moving van! Roll it!

204
00:11:07.233 --> 00:11:09.466
Get ready to be bedazzled!

205
00:11:13.466 --> 00:11:15.300
Acting!

206
00:11:16.300 --> 00:11:19.800
Acting!

207
00:11:19.866 --> 00:11:21.900
All the world’s a stage!

208
00:11:21.966 --> 00:11:26.100
And no actress stages more worldliness than I, Jessilana!

209
00:11:26.166 --> 00:11:28.166
Now, may I count on you?

210
00:11:28.233 --> 00:11:31.166
Of course I’m assuming that all of you can count.

211
00:11:31.233 --> 00:11:34.100
I’ve never seen anything like this before.

212
00:11:34.166 --> 00:11:36.000
Yeah and I’m kind of glad.

213
00:11:36.066 --> 00:11:39.366
Well, at least their video’s been edited and they have a soundtrack!

214
00:11:39.433 --> 00:11:41.766
- Yeah, so should we ask them?
- Pikachu!

215
00:11:41.833 --> 00:11:44.366
Guess so. Will you help us with our video?

216
00:11:44.433 --> 00:11:45.733
We thought you’d never ask.

217
00:11:45.800 --> 00:11:49.033
We’ve already got the footage, so we just need it to be edited

218
00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:51.433
- and the sound added in.
- What?

219
00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:54.433
-Who do you posers think you are?

220
00:11:54.500 --> 00:11:59.366
I’m an accomplished makeup artist as well as a great actress. So there.

221
00:11:59.433 --> 00:12:02.166
I’m the great Pokévision producer, Jamecetti!

222
00:12:02.233 --> 00:12:04.466
And I’m the number one director, Spielmeowth!

223
00:12:04.533 --> 00:12:06.900
Do you really think professionals like us

224
00:12:06.966 --> 00:12:09.500
would use footage taken by amateurs the likes of you?

225
00:12:09.566 --> 00:12:12.333
There’s no dispute. We must reshoot!

226
00:12:13.933 --> 00:12:15.699
Now...

227
00:12:15.766 --> 00:12:17.833
- We’ll need these!
- Yes.

228
00:12:17.900 --> 00:12:19.400
Okay, but what about us?

229
00:12:19.466 --> 00:12:21.233
And what are you going to use for costumes?

230
00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:23.833
It would be great to be able to watch you guys work.

231
00:12:23.900 --> 00:12:28.000
Oh, costumes and scenery will be computer generated, so no worries.

232
00:12:28.066 --> 00:12:32.066
And we need complete concentration while we work, so there will be no peeking!

233
00:12:32.133 --> 00:12:34.033
Now, chill and wait out here.

234
00:12:34.099 --> 00:12:36.433
- Something doesn’t feel right!
- Agreed!

235
00:12:36.500 --> 00:12:38.333
- Yeah.
- Let’s go take a look!

236
00:12:41.166 --> 00:12:42.433
Huh?

237
00:12:42.500 --> 00:12:44.866
- What?!
- It’s an empty room!

238
00:12:44.933 --> 00:12:47.233
- Fenn!
- Fennekin!

239
00:12:47.300 --> 00:12:49.099
Huh?

240
00:12:50.666 --> 00:12:53.833
Look! That balloon!

241
00:12:53.900 --> 00:12:56.366
Prepare for trouble! Your vision is good!

242
00:12:56.433 --> 00:12:58.833
Too bad your heads are made out of wood.

243
00:12:58.900 --> 00:13:01.400
To protect the world from devastation!

244
00:13:01.466 --> 00:13:04.199
To unite all people within our nation!

245
00:13:04.266 --> 00:13:07.433
To denounce the evils of truth and love!

246
00:13:07.500 --> 00:13:10.366
To extend our reach to the stars above!

247
00:13:10.433 --> 00:13:12.866
- Jessie!
- And James!

248
00:13:12.933 --> 00:13:15.933
Team Rocket blasts off at the speed of light!

249
00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:19.033
Surrender now or prepare for one cinematic fight!

250
00:13:19.099 --> 00:13:22.233
- Meowth, that’s right!
- Wobbuffet!

251
00:13:25.699 --> 00:13:27.633
Team Rocket! Not you again!

252
00:13:27.699 --> 00:13:31.900
Hm. I wouldn’t be surprised if they broke the editing machine!

253
00:13:31.966 --> 00:13:33.900
Well, well, I wonder.

254
00:13:33.966 --> 00:13:36.433
- Give Fennekin back!
- Dedenne, too!

255
00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:39.866
- And Pikachu!
- Not on your life! We’re flying high!

256
00:13:39.933 --> 00:13:42.099
Bye!

257
00:13:42.166 --> 00:13:45.533
No way! Fletchling! I choose you!

258
00:13:47.133 --> 00:13:48.400
Fletchling!

259
00:13:48.466 --> 00:13:51.466
- Go after Team Rocket!
- Fletch! Fletch!

260
00:13:53.533 --> 00:13:55.466
Fletch! Fletch, Fletch, Fletchling!

261
00:13:58.000 --> 00:14:01.033
Pika Pi!

262
00:14:02.033 --> 00:14:04.699
To the Pikachu we’ve been chasing for so long!

263
00:14:04.766 --> 00:14:06.000
And let’s not forget

264
00:14:06.066 --> 00:14:10.099
we were able to catch the other twerp Pokémon for little more than a song!

265
00:14:10.166 --> 00:14:12.699
Team Rocket’s strong!

266
00:14:12.766 --> 00:14:15.699
So now that that little project is off the table,

267
00:14:15.766 --> 00:14:19.366
time to start work on our next Pokévision production!

268
00:14:19.433 --> 00:14:22.966
- Are you serious?
- But we already wrapped that project!

269
00:14:23.033 --> 00:14:25.699
I’m an actress and an actress must act!

270
00:14:25.766 --> 00:14:29.866
So! Off we go to make a brand new Jessilana video show!

271
00:14:29.933 --> 00:14:31.766
Now!

272
00:14:32.766 --> 00:14:35.699
Acting. It’s the craft of a lifetime!

273
00:14:35.766 --> 00:14:41.199
To be or not to be the greatest actress of them all! Now, that is the question!

274
00:14:41.266 --> 00:14:43.566
Whether she’s lost her mind is the question.

275
00:14:43.633 --> 00:14:45.433
The jury’s out on that one.

276
00:14:45.500 --> 00:14:47.966
Wobbuffet!

277
00:14:50.833 --> 00:14:53.366
Fletchling!

278
00:14:53.433 --> 00:14:56.666
Fletch! Fletch!

279
00:14:56.733 --> 00:14:59.866
- So, did you find Team Rocket?
- Fletch! Fletchling!

280
00:14:59.933 --> 00:15:03.433
- Awesome! Show us where they are!
- Fletchling!

281
00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:06.599
Chu! Pika! Pikachu!

282
00:15:06.666 --> 00:15:09.400
Na! Na! Na! Na!

283
00:15:09.466 --> 00:15:11.099
Na! Oh!

284
00:15:11.166 --> 00:15:15.199
Fennekin!

285
00:15:15.266 --> 00:15:17.800
-Pikachu!

286
00:15:17.866 --> 00:15:19.166
- Pika!
- Fennekin!

287
00:15:21.133 --> 00:15:22.300
- Huh?
- Pika! Pika!

288
00:15:22.366 --> 00:15:24.800
- Na! Na!
- Pikachu!

289
00:15:28.500 --> 00:15:30.800
- Huh?

290
00:15:30.866 --> 00:15:32.766
Pikachu!

291
00:15:32.833 --> 00:15:34.033
Pika, Pika!

292
00:15:34.099 --> 00:15:36.433
- Fennekin!
- Pika?

293
00:15:36.500 --> 00:15:37.699
Fennekin!

294
00:15:37.766 --> 00:15:40.000
- Fennekin!
- You’re all okay!

295
00:15:40.066 --> 00:15:43.000
Why is it only raining over there?

296
00:15:43.066 --> 00:15:45.599
It looks like the twerps are crashing our set!

297
00:15:45.666 --> 00:15:47.433
We’ve got Pokémon problems!

298
00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:51.066
What? Can’t you see I’m busy making movie magic up here?

299
00:15:51.133 --> 00:15:54.199
Take Pikachu and the rest of your paltry Pokémon!

300
00:15:54.266 --> 00:15:56.733
She is good at acting like a fool!

301
00:15:56.800 --> 00:15:58.766
- Pikapi!
- Pikachu!

302
00:15:58.833 --> 00:16:00.599
Dedenne!

303
00:16:00.666 --> 00:16:02.666
- Pika! Pika!
- Huh?

304
00:16:02.733 --> 00:16:07.300
I should have known. Fennekin hates to get dirty, like me!

305
00:16:07.366 --> 00:16:09.466
- Serena?
- Fennekin!

306
00:16:09.533 --> 00:16:13.933
No. No way! Inkay! Use Psybeam on the twerpette!

307
00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:16.466
Inkay!

308
00:16:16.533 --> 00:16:19.366
-Fenn!

309
00:16:19.433 --> 00:16:21.666
Fenn!

310
00:16:23.099 --> 00:16:26.500
Who cares about dirty clothes?

311
00:16:26.566 --> 00:16:29.900
Fennekin has always been there to protect me!

312
00:16:29.966 --> 00:16:31.933
Hm!

313
00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:35.433
Your cue, Pumpkaboo! Shadow Ball!

314
00:16:35.500 --> 00:16:38.400
Pumpkaboo!

315
00:16:38.466 --> 00:16:44.266
- Now, Pikachu, Thunderbolt!
- Pika! Pikachu!

316
00:16:47.566 --> 00:16:50.400
I don’t care if I get dirty or not!

317
00:16:50.466 --> 00:16:53.566
This time it’s my turn to protect you!

318
00:16:53.633 --> 00:16:55.533
Fenn!

319
00:16:55.599 --> 00:16:57.733
Kin!

320
00:16:57.800 --> 00:16:59.966
Fenn, Fenn! Fennekin!

321
00:17:01.699 --> 00:17:05.000
Fenn, Fenn! Fennekin!

322
00:17:15.399 --> 00:17:18.333
Fenn! Fenn!

323
00:17:18.399 --> 00:17:21.866
- Thank goodness you’re okay!
- Kin!

324
00:17:21.933 --> 00:17:24.833
- Aw! Your fur’s a mess!
- Fenn!

325
00:17:26.666 --> 00:17:29.766
Inkay, show the twerps we will not be shunned!

326
00:17:29.833 --> 00:17:31.300
Inkay!

327
00:17:31.366 --> 00:17:33.533
Electro Ball! Let's go!

328
00:17:33.600 --> 00:17:37.333
Pika! Pika, Pika, Pika, Pika! Chupi!

329
00:17:38.566 --> 00:17:42.633
The job of this great actress is showing a clueless twerpette the ropes!

330
00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:46.066
Now! Pumpkaboo, use Frustration on the two of them!

331
00:17:46.133 --> 00:17:49.100
Pump, Pump, Pump! Boo!

332
00:17:49.166 --> 00:17:50.566
Fennekin!

333
00:17:50.633 --> 00:17:51.800
Pump, Pump, Pump!

334
00:17:51.866 --> 00:17:54.300
Fennekin!

335
00:17:54.366 --> 00:17:57.233
- Whoa! What’s that?!
- Flamethrower! Wow!

336
00:17:59.600 --> 00:18:03.333
Huh? That's unbelievable! You just learned Flamethrower!

337
00:18:03.399 --> 00:18:05.000
- Great job!
- Kin!

338
00:18:05.066 --> 00:18:07.966
All right, then, Pikachu, use Thunderbolt!

339
00:18:08.033 --> 00:18:12.800
Pika! Pikachu!

340
00:18:17.733 --> 00:18:20.266
We’re blasting off again!

341
00:18:20.333 --> 00:18:22.633
Wobbuffet!

342
00:18:24.233 --> 00:18:26.833
We did it! We did it!

343
00:18:30.333 --> 00:18:32.166
Fennekin!

344
00:18:39.633 --> 00:18:43.066
- You’re all clean again, Fennekin!
- Fenn!

345
00:18:43.133 --> 00:18:46.666
- Serena, the Pokévision video’s done!
- Hm. I’m coming!

346
00:18:46.733 --> 00:18:49.666
- Fenn!
- Sorry to keep you waiting!

347
00:18:49.733 --> 00:18:52.766
All right, now, let me show you your finished video.

348
00:18:52.833 --> 00:18:54.500
Great! Thank you!

349
00:18:57.566 --> 00:19:01.733
Hi! My name’s Serena and this is my partner, Fennekin!

350
00:19:03.533 --> 00:19:06.666
We love making sweet treats!

351
00:19:06.733 --> 00:19:09.200
And we love eating them, too!

352
00:19:12.133 --> 00:19:15.566
We also love to dress up and look our best!

353
00:19:18.766 --> 00:19:22.766
If you see us around, please stop and say hi, okay?

354
00:19:28.133 --> 00:19:30.833
- You both looked so great!
- Thanks, Bonnie!

355
00:19:30.899 --> 00:19:33.566
- Pretty nice, I must say!
- Chespin! Pin-Pin!

356
00:19:33.633 --> 00:19:38.066
I guess pretty nice is sort of a compliment. Hey Ash, what did you think?

357
00:19:38.133 --> 00:19:40.933
Who, me? I thought it was awesome!

358
00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:42.566
- Pika!
- Chespin! Ches!

359
00:19:42.633 --> 00:19:48.399
- Really? Fennekin, did you hear that?
- Fenn! Nekin!

360
00:19:49.399 --> 00:19:52.066
Thanks to Pokévision, the bond between Serena

361
00:19:52.133 --> 00:19:54.399
and Fennekin is there for all to see,

362
00:19:54.466 --> 00:19:58.133
as our heroes’ journey to Cyllage City continues!

363
00:20:01.366 --> 00:20:03.766
Hello there! My name’s Clemont.

364
00:20:03.833 --> 00:20:05.866
I’d like you to meet my partners,

365
00:20:05.933 --> 00:20:07.300
- Chespin...
- Ches!

366
00:20:07.366 --> 00:20:09.633
- ..and Bunnelby!
- Bun!

367
00:20:09.700 --> 00:20:14.333
I’m a handsome Gym Leader from the Lumiose City Gym!

368
00:20:14.399 --> 00:20:19.033
I can be shy, but I’m very strong in my own gentle way!

369
00:20:19.100 --> 00:20:23.366
I love to invent things and right now I’m looking for a nice girl

370
00:20:23.433 --> 00:20:25.899
- who I can be a good friend to.
- Chespin!

371
00:20:25.966 --> 00:20:27.533
Hey, out of the way!

372
00:20:27.600 --> 00:20:29.833
Bunnelby!

373
00:20:29.899 --> 00:20:32.233
Hey! There’s no reason for you two to have a fight!

374
00:20:32.300 --> 00:20:34.066
Stop it right now!

375
00:20:35.833 --> 00:20:37.666
Chespin!

376
00:20:40.500 --> 00:20:43.633
- That’s my big brother!
- Ches!

377
00:20:43.700 --> 00:20:45.700
Huh?
